content:
Current-source comparison for direct-input spec.md AC-1/AC-2/AC-3.
This is source inspection, not a browser run, visual QA or independent review.

AC-1: spec.md requests a labelled All/Active/Archived/Paused selector above the list,
matching API results and count. app.js imports existing selectField, creates the
Status label/options inside #toolbar (which index.html places above #rows), updates
status, calls the unchanged projects API client and displays singular/plural count.
Node tests cover the real event handlers, relative request URLs, row content/count.
Local integration uses the real server and actual app/api/ui modules under an
explicitly simulated DOM. It verifies real all/active/archived/paused responses.

AC-2: selected is separate from visible. Only the row selection callback changes
selection.textContent. The request, empty and error paths do not change selected
or that panel. renderRows receives selected?.id after each successful filter.
Empty success has No projects found. plus 0 projects; error has existing alert and
Retry with blank result count. Node and real-API integration assert Tide survives
archived/paused and its aria-pressed state returns under active/all.

AC-3 and ux.md: load marks aria-busy and displays loading separately. showProblem
is the original helper. Retry calls load using current status. The monotonic
latestRequest check protects success, error and finally, so obsolete responses
cannot change rows/count or clear current loading. Tests include initial failure,
network rejection, retry, stale success/failure and stale completion during loading.
The real server run toggles ONLY the documented synthetic fixture mode endpoint,
observes HTTP 503, restores fail=false and verifies Retry recovery.

DESIGN.md vs selected prototype: keep two-column layout and list/aside order from
the supplied shell, switching to one column below 700px. Add flex filter/count row
and wrapping with --space. Keep app --accent #2053e8 (blue), --surface, --line and
--space; the prototype orange demo accent is intentionally not applied as DESIGN
requires. Existing native labelled select, button row helpers and :focus-visible
rule are retained. Static inspection establishes code structure and token use;
actual wide/narrow layout, keyboard focus, accessible announcements and browser
interaction still require an available browser. No screenshots were fabricated.

Repository check: git diff --check exit_code=0 (actual invocation recorded in tool trace).
Initial untracked user-draft.md is preserved; supplied documents, index, server,
API client and UI helpers have no changes. Helper assessment checks bytes/scope.

--- src/app.js (current exact lines) ---
1: import { projects } from './api.js';
2: import { renderRows, selectField, showProblem } from './ui.js';
3: 
4: const toolbar = document.querySelector('#toolbar');
5: const rows = document.querySelector('#rows');
6: const selection = document.querySelector('#selection');
7: const count = document.createElement('span');
8: count.setAttribute('role', 'status');
9: count.setAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');
10: rows.setAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');
11: 
12: let status = 'all';
13: let selected = null;
14: let visible = [];
15: let latestRequest = 0;
16: 
17: toolbar.className = 'filter';
18: toolbar.append(selectField({
19:   label: 'Status',
20:   options: [['all', 'All'], ['active', 'Active'], ['archived', 'Archived'], ['paused', 'Paused']],
21:   value: status,
22:   onChange(value) {
23:     status = value;
24:     void load();
25:   }
26: }), count);
27: 
28: function render() {
29:   if (visible.length === 0) {
30:     rows.textContent = 'No projects found.';
31:     return;
32:   }
33:   renderRows(rows, visible, selected?.id, project => {
34:     selected = project;
35:     selection.textContent = project.name;
36:     render();
37:   });
38: }
39: 
40: async function load() {
41:   const request = ++latestRequest;
42:   rows.setAttribute('aria-busy', 'true');
43:   rows.textContent = 'Loading projects…';
44:   count.textContent = 'Loading…';
45:   try {
46:     const result = await projects(status);
47:     if (request !== latestRequest) return;
48:     visible = result;
49:     count.textContent = `${visible.length} ${visible.length === 1 ? 'project' : 'projects'}`;
50:     render();
51:   } catch {
52:     if (request !== latestRequest) return;
53:     count.textContent = '';
54:     showProblem(rows, () => { void load(); });
55:   } finally {
56:     if (request === latestRequest) rows.setAttribute('aria-busy', 'false');
57:   }
58: }
59: 
60: await load();

--- src/theme.css (current exact lines) ---
1: :root{--accent:#2053e8;--surface:#fff;--line:#d8dee9;--space:12px}
2: body{font:16px system-ui;margin:32px;background:#f6f7fa;color:#182230}header{margin-bottom:24px}
3: .layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr;gap:24px}.panel{background:var(--surface);padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px}
4: .filter{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--space);flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:calc(var(--space)*2)}
5: button,select{font:inherit;padding:10px;border-radius:6px}button{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);cursor:pointer}
6: select{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface)}
7: .project{display:block;margin:var(--space) 0;width:100%;text-align:left}.project[aria-pressed=true]{border:2px solid var(--accent)}
8: :focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:3px}.problem{border-left:3px solid var(--accent);padding:var(--space)}
9: @media(max-width:700px){.layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}body{margin:16px}}

--- src/ui.js (current exact lines) ---
1: export function selectField({ label, options, value, onChange }) {
2:   const wrapper = document.createElement('label');
3:   wrapper.append(document.createTextNode(`${label} `));
4:   const select = document.createElement('select');
5:   for (const [key, title] of options) select.add(new Option(title, key));
6:   select.value = value;
7:   select.addEventListener('change', () => onChange(select.value));
8:   wrapper.append(select);
9:   return wrapper;
10: }
11: 
12: export function renderRows(container, rows, selectedId, onSelect) {
13:   container.replaceChildren();
14:   for (const row of rows) {
15:     const button = document.createElement('button');
16:     button.className = 'project'; button.dataset.projectId = row.id;
17:     button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(selectedId === row.id));
18:     button.textContent = `${row.name} — ${row.status}`;
19:     button.addEventListener('click', () => onSelect(row));
20:     container.append(button);
21:   }
22: }
23: 
24: export function showProblem(container, retry) {
25:   const problem = document.createElement('div'); problem.className = 'problem';
26:   problem.setAttribute('role', 'alert'); problem.append('Could not load projects. ');
27:   const button = document.createElement('button'); button.textContent = 'Retry';
28:   button.addEventListener('click', retry); problem.append(button);
29:   container.replaceChildren(problem);
30: }

--- src/api.js (current exact lines) ---
1: export async function projects(status = 'all') {
2:   const response = await fetch(`/api/projects?status=${encodeURIComponent(status)}`);
3:   if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Could not load projects');
4:   return response.json();
5: }

--- index.html (current exact lines) ---
1: <!doctype html>
2: <html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
3: <title>Projects</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/src/theme.css">
4: <header><h1>Projects</h1><p>Browse projects and keep one selected while filtering.</p></header>
5: <main class="layout"><section class="panel"><div id="toolbar"></div><div id="rows"></div></section>
6: <aside class="panel"><h2>Selected project</h2><p id="selection">None</p></aside></main>
7: <script type="module" src="/src/app.js"></script></html>

--- spec.md (current exact lines) ---
1: # Project list implementation
2: 
3: - AC-1: Add a labelled status selector above the list: All, Active, Archived, Paused.
4:   Changing it fetches that status through the existing API client and shows matching
5:   projects and their result count. Use the selected reference's structure.
6: - AC-2: A project can be selected and its name appears in the selected-project panel.
7:   Keep the selection when filtering hides that project. Filtering back restores the
8:   selected appearance. A successful empty result has its own visible empty state.
9: - AC-3: A failed request has the existing error treatment and Retry action, distinct
10:   from an empty success. Retry uses the current filter and preserves the selection.
11:   The current implementation must not be reported browser-verified without opening it.
12: 
13: Use DESIGN.md and ux.md. Implement in src/ and tests/. The server and contracts are
14: provided infrastructure. Do not commit, push, post, install packages, or edit the
15: input documents/user draft. Record evidence outside this application.

--- DESIGN.md (current exact lines) ---
1: # Project workspace
2: 
3: Use the existing --accent, --surface, --line and --space tokens. The app accent is
4: blue. The selected reference governs structure; its orange demo accent is not a
5: system-token override. On wide screens, show the list and selected-project panel
6: side by side; on narrow screens, put the selected-project panel below the list.
7: Controls need visible labels and keyboard focus. Preserve existing UI helpers.

--- ux.md (current exact lines) ---
1: # Existing list patterns
2: 
3: Use selectField for a labelled selector, renderRows for project rows, and
4: showProblem for the error/retry treatment. Keep the selected project in application
5: state independently of the currently visible list. Show loading separately from
6: empty/error; do not clear the selected-project panel on a request or an error.
7: If filters change during loading, only the latest selection's response may render.
8: 
9: The server's PUT /__fixture__/mode endpoint controls only this synthetic fixture:
10: JSON {"fail":true} makes subsequent API requests fail; {"fail":false} restores them.
11: This endpoint is evaluation infrastructure, not a production feature or UI control.
